<h2>Part 2. Who Hires It</h2>

<h3>Family celebrations</h3>
<p>Anniversaries, birthdays, housewarmings and reunions are the most common uses. A group of 10 to 12 relatives fits comfortably, with room for older family members to stretch out. The wide seats and curtains also help children nap on long drives.</p>

<h3>Multi-generational holidays</h3>
<p>Three generations on one holiday need a vehicle that suits everyone. Grandparents want space and a steady ride, parents want everyone together, and children want windows and snacks. The Maharaja layout serves all three. See <a href="/services/family-tours">family tours</a> and <a href="/services/resort-trips">resort trips</a>.</p>

<h3>Milestone trips</h3>
<p>Retirement trips, golden anniversaries and pilgrimages for senior relatives are better in a roomy vehicle. Fewer seats mean fewer people to coordinate and more time to enjoy the journey.</p>

<h3>Small corporate groups</h3>
<p>Teams of 10 to 12 use it for offsites and client visits where a comfortable, private cabin matters but a luxury van is not needed. A GST invoice is available. See <a href="/services/corporate-travel">corporate travel</a>.</p>

<h3>Wedding family transport</h3>
<p>For wedding days, a Maharaja Tempo Traveller takes an immediate family group between the hotel, the venue and the reception. See <a href="/services/wedding-transportation">wedding transportation</a>.</p>

<h3>Pilgrimage groups</h3>
<p>Groups of 10 to 12 on Tirupati, Mantralaya or Dharmasthala trips value the room to rest between long temple queues. See <a href="/services/pilgrimage-tours">pilgrimage tours</a>.</p>

<h2>Part 3. Seating and Luggage for a Group of 12</h2>

<h3>A seating plan</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Front seats:</strong> elderly relatives and anyone prone to motion sickness.</li>
<li><strong>Middle seats:</strong> families with small children, close to the aisle.</li>
<li><strong>Rear seats:</strong> teenagers and able adults who can handle the extra movement.</li>
</ul>
<p>Rotate seats at lunch on a long trip so nobody sits at the back all day.</p>

<h3>Luggage</h3>
<p>Because the seating takes more space, luggage room is a little tighter than on a standard Traveller. Count your bags before booking. Soft bags travel best. Keep documents, medicines, jewellery and electronics in the cabin. If you carry more luggage than a group of 12 would normally bring, tell us so we can confirm what fits, or suggest the <a href="/fleet/tempo-traveller/tempo-traveller-17-seater">17 seater Tempo Traveller</a>.</p>

<h3>Cabin habits that keep it comfortable</h3>
<ul>
<li>Keep the aisle clear.</li>
<li>Use headphones for personal media.</li>
<li>Avoid strongly scented food.</li>
<li>Agree on curtains and AC settings together.</li>
<li>Take wrappers and bottles with you at stops.</li>
</ul>

