<h2>Part 5. Trip Ideas for a Group of 12</h2>

<h3>One day: Mysore</h3>
<p>Leave at 6:30 AM. Breakfast on the highway, then the Mysore Palace, Chamundi Hills and lunch in the city. Visit Brindavan Gardens or the markets in the afternoon, and return in the evening. The round trip is under 300 km, so the 300 km daily minimum is billed, about ₹7,100 before extras.</p>

<h3>Two days: Coorg</h3>
<p>Day one, drive to Coorg with a stop at Namdroling Monastery at Bylakuppe. Visit Abbey Falls and Raja's Seat. Day two, see Dubare or Talacauvery, shop for coffee and spices in Madikeri and return. About 600 km is billed, about ₹14,200 before extras. See the <a href="/tour-packages/coorg-getaway">Coorg Getaway</a> and the <a href="/blog/bangalore-to-coorg-road-trip-itinerary-tempo-traveller">Coorg itinerary</a>.</p>

<h3>Two days: Chikmagalur</h3>
<p>Day one, drive to a coffee-estate stay. Day two, go early to Mullayanagiri or Baba Budangiri, see Hebbe Falls and return. See the <a href="/tour-packages/chikmagalur-coffee-trails">Chikmagalur Coffee Trails</a> and the <a href="/blog/bangalore-to-chikmagalur-weekend-road-trip-guide">Chikmagalur guide</a>.</p>

<h3>Three days: Ooty and Coonoor</h3>
<p>Drive to Ooty in daylight so the forest check-posts are crossed before they close at night. Visit the Botanical Garden, the lake, Doddabetta and tea estates around Coonoor, and return on day three. See the <a href="/tour-packages/ooty-coonoor-hill-tour">Ooty and Coonoor Hill Tour</a>.</p>

<h3>Three days: Wayanad</h3>
<p>Drive to Wayanad, visit Edakkal Caves, Banasura Sagar and Soochipara Falls, and return. Interstate permits apply as the route enters Kerala. See the <a href="/tour-packages/wayanad-nature-escape">Wayanad Nature Escape</a>.</p>

<h3>Three days: Hampi</h3>
<p>Drive to Hampi, spend a full day at the Virupaksha temple, the Vittala temple and the Royal Enclosure, and return. About 900 km is billed, about ₹21,300 before extras. See the <a href="/tour-packages/hampi-heritage-trail">Hampi Heritage Trail</a>.</p>

