<h2>Part 6. Planning Tips</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Fix the headcount.</strong> Twelve is the limit. For 13 or more, choose the <a href="/fleet/tempo-traveller/tempo-traveller-17-seater">17 seater</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Choose one coordinator</strong> who handles the driver, the list and the receipts.</li>
<li><strong>Plan the pickups.</strong> One meeting point is faster than many doorstep stops. Area pages include <a href="/12seater-tempotraveller/whitefield">Whitefield</a>, <a href="/12seater-tempotraveller/koramangala">Koramangala</a>, <a href="/12seater-tempotraveller/indiranagar">Indiranagar</a> and <a href="/12seater-tempotraveller/hebbal">Hebbal</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Start early.</strong> A 5:00 or 6:00 AM start avoids the worst traffic and protects daylight on hill roads.</li>
<li><strong>Leave room for stops.</strong> A group of 12 needs half an hour for breakfast and an hour for lunch.</li>
<li><strong>Get the quotation in writing,</strong> with the rate, daily minimum, Bata and expected extras.</li>
<li><strong>Confirm the vehicle and driver</strong> a day before.</li>
</ol>

<h2>Part 7. Comfort and Safety</h2>
<ul>
<li>Wear seat belts where fitted. Keep the aisle clear and do not stand while moving.</li>
<li>Ask for a break every two hours, and listen if the driver advises against a late-night dash.</li>
<li>For elderly travellers, seat them in front and carry glucose, water and medicines.</li>
<li>For children, bring wipes, snacks and a motion-sickness plan.</li>
<li>In monsoon, allow slack in the schedule for slower roads.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Part 8. When to Travel</h2>
<p>November to February is the best season for almost every destination and the busiest for weddings and holidays. March to May suits hill stations such as Ooty and Coorg, and AC is worth taking. June to September brings green hills and waterfalls with slower roads. October is a good month for festival trips. Book early for weekends and long weekends.</p>

<h2>Part 9. Mistakes to Avoid</h2>
<ol>
<li>Booking a 12 seater for 13 people.</li>
<li>Not counting bags.</li>
<li>Choosing non-AC for a summer plains trip.</li>
<li>Comparing only the per-km rate.</li>
<li>Returning after 10:00 PM and paying extra Bata.</li>
<li>Skipping the written quotation.</li>
<li>Forgetting interstate permits for Tirupati, Ooty or Wayanad.</li>
<li>Booking late for peak dates.</li>
</ol>

